        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-19 for Mission Bay's third real-buildings pass (remaining uncovered footprints inside the official Mission Bay North/South redevelopment-area boundary): 500 Terry A. Francois Blvd (Mission Bay Block 26A), a 6-story, ~310,000 sq ft office building built by the Sobrato Organization, completed 2008; sat empty for four years before Cisco's Meraki division leased space in 2012, followed by Cisco's $1.2B acquisition of Meraki. Tenants have included Cisco and Wix. CORRECTED 2026-09-19: this file originally used only 1 of 3 real DataSF footprint pieces sharing mblr SF8721010 (the smallest, ~1172 sq m) -- a satellite-imagery cross-check prompted by the owner questioning apparent gaps elsewhere on the map led to a systematic real-city-block coverage audit, which caught this building's own incomplete geometry. Corrected to the union of all 3 pieces (~8636 sq m total), matching the ~310,000 sq ft / 6-story building described in sourcing.",
